('useful','可以有效擦除。','Useful erase allowed.'),('blocked','仍有冲突，不能擦除。','Conflict remains; cannot erase.'),('noop','没有新字母，跳过。','No new letters; skip.'),
('wrong','诱人的错误规则：“只要有一个字母吻合就擦除。”反例 stamp=ab、target=aba：起点 0 擦成 ??a；起点 1 虽有 ?，但末尾 a 与印章 b 冲突，不能擦。忽略冲突会错误地报告成功。只找完全相等的子串也不行：a?? 已无完整 ab，却仍然可擦。','Tempting wrong rule: “erase if even one letter matches.” Counterexample stamp=ab, target=aba: erase start 0 to get ??a. Start 1 has a ?, but its final a conflicts with stamp letter b. Ignoring that conflict falsely reports success. Requiring an exact substring is also wrong: a?? contains no full ab, yet it can be erased.'),
('baselineTitle','基线：反复扫描每个窗口','Baseline: rescan every window'),
('baselineText','基线每轮检查所有起点，每个检查比较 m 个字符。每个有进展的轮次至少擦一个字母，因此最多 n 轮，最坏 O(n²m) 时间、O(n) 辅助空间。n=1000 时这个上界可达十亿级字符检查。前向穷举也正确，但要搜索大量不同字符串；测试用它做小规模独立核对。','The baseline checks every start each round, comparing m characters per check. Every productive round erases at least one letter, so there are at most n rounds: O(n²m) time and O(n) auxiliary space. At n=1000 that bound reaches a billion character checks. Forward exhaustive search is also correct but explores many distinct strings; tests use it as an independent small-case check.'),
('h2','擦掉一个位置，能解锁哪些窗口？','Which windows does one erased position unlock?'),
('p2','窗口 i 是起点为 i 的 m 个格子，m 为印章长度。阻塞位置：某窗口中与印章不符、而且还没擦掉的位置。todo[i] 数窗口 i 的剩余阻塞位置；waiting[p] 列出最初被位置 p 阻塞的窗口。aab 配 ab 时，窗口 0 只有位置 1 阻塞，todo=[1,0]、waiting[1]=[0]。窗口 1 先擦位置 1、2，位置 1 让 todo[0] 从 1 减到 0；窗口 0 就解锁了。无需重扫所有窗口。','Window i covers m cells from start i, where m is stamp length. A blocker is an unerased position whose original letter disagrees with the stamp in that window. todo[i] counts window i’s remaining blockers; waiting[p] lists windows originally blocked by position p. For ab and aab, only position 1 blocks window 0: todo=[1,0], waiting[1]=[0]. Window 1 erases positions 1 and 2. Position 1 reduces todo[0] from 1 to 0, unlocking window 0 without rescanning all windows.'),
('queueText','队列是先进先出的待处理列表；初始放入 todo=0 的窗口。每次取出一个窗口，把尚未擦除的格子标记 done，再沿 waiting 更新计数；某个计数刚变 0 就入队。计数为 0 只说明无冲突，窗口可能已全被擦过，此时跳过、不记答案。','A queue processes ready items in first-in, first-out order. Initially enqueue windows with todo=0. Pop a window, mark its new erasures in done, and update counts along waiting. Enqueue a window exactly when its count becomes 0. Zero means no conflicts, but the whole window may already be erased; then skip it without recording an answer.'),
('invariant','为什么能任意选择就绪窗口？不变式是每次操作后仍成立的事实：未擦字母始终等于目标字母，todo 恰好数未擦的原始冲突。擦除只删除约束，不会让别的窗口更难擦。任何尚可完成的反向过程，其下一次有效擦除必有零冲突窗口。因此队列耗尽仍留字母就无解；擦空后倒序还原，每戳在仍受约束的位置都写对字母，被忽略的位置会被后续戳覆盖。','Why may we choose any ready window? An invariant is a fact preserved after each operation: visible letters equal their target letters, and todo counts exactly the unerased original conflicts. Erasing only removes constraints, so it cannot make another window harder to erase. Any reverse process that can still finish must have a conflict-free useful next erase. Thus an empty queue with letters remaining proves impossibility. If everything is erased, replay in reverse: each stamp writes the correct constrained letters, while later stamps overwrite the positions that were ignored.'),
('observe2','切换预设会把本实验重置。逐次处理队首，观察下表计数与历史中的减法；上一个／重置恢复完整快照。格子上行是字母，下行是位置；? 是已擦，边框和“本次”文字只标记刚处理的窗口。','Changing a preset resets this experiment. Process queue heads and watch the counts and subtraction ledger. Back/reset restore full snapshots. Cells show letters above positions; ? means erased. A border and the “current” text identify only the window just processed.'),
